\n  \"action\": \"/tool_runner/index\",\n  \"citations\": true,\n  \"creator\": null,\n  \"credentials\": [],\n  \"description\": \"Assess genome assembly and annotation completeness\",\n  \"display\": true,\n  \"edam_operations\": [],\n  \"edam_topics\": [],\n  \"enctype\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\",\n  \"errors\": {},\n  \"form_style\": \"regular\",\n  \"has_parameters\": true,\n  \"help\": \"<div class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"busco-assessing-genome-assembly-and-annotation-completeness-with-benchmarking-universal-single-copy-orthologs\\\">\\n<h1>BUSCO: Assessing genome assembly and annotation completeness with Benchmarking Universal Single-Copy Orthologs</h1>\\n<div class=\\\"section\\\" id=\\\"interpreting-the-results\\\">\\n<h2>Interpreting the results</h2>\\n<p><a class=\\\"reference external\\\" href=\\\"http://busco.ezlab.org/\\\">BUSCO</a> attempts to provide a quantitative assessment of the completeness in terms of the expected gene content of a\\ngenome assembly, transcriptome, or annotated gene set. The results are simplified into categories of Complete\\nand single-copy, Complete and duplicated, Fragmented, or Missing BUSCOs.</p>\\n<p>BUSCO completeness results make sense only in the context of the biology of your organism.\\nYou have to understand whether missing or duplicated genes are of biological or technical origin.\\nFor instance, a high level of duplication may be explained by a recent whole duplication event\\n(biological) or a chimeric assembly of haplotypes (technical).\\nTranscriptomes and protein sets that are not filtered for isoforms will lead to a high proportion of duplicates.\\nTherefore you should filter them before a BUSCO analysis.\\nFinally, focusing on specific tissues or specific life stages and conditions in a transcriptomic experiment\\nis unlikely to produce a BUSCO-complete transcriptome. In this case, consistency across your samples\\nis what you will be aiming for.</p>\\n<p>For more information please refer to the <a class=\\\"reference external\\\" href=\\\"http://busco.ezlab.org/\\\">Busco</a> <a class=\\\"reference external\\\" href=\\\"https://busco.ezlab.org/busco_userguide.html#interpreting-the-results\\\">user guide</a>\\n.</p>\\n</div>\\n</div>\\n\",\n  \"help_format\": \"restructuredtext\",\n  \"hidden\": \"\",\n  \"hidden_versions\": [],\n  \"history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b539ded258ff742634\",\n  \"icon\": null,\n  \"id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/iuc/busco/busco/6.1.0+galaxy0\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"argument\": null,\n      \"default_value\": null,\n      \"help\": \"\",\n      \"help_format\": \"html\",\n      \"hidden\": true,\n      \"is_dynamic\": false,\n      \"label\": \"\",\n      \"model_class\": \"HiddenToolParameter\",\n      \"name\": \"test\",\n      \"optional\": false,\n      \"refresh_on_change\": false,\n      \"text_value\": \"Not available.\",\n      \"type\": \"hidden\",\n      \"value\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"argument\": null,\n      \"default_value\": {\n        \"values\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721353c9efc12d8588209\",\n            \"src\": \"hda\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"edam\": {\n        \"edam_data\": [\n          \"data_2044\",\n          \"data_2044\"\n        ],\n        \"edam_formats\": [\n          \"format_1929\",\n          \"format_1929\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"extensions\": [\n        \"fasta\",\n        \"fasta.gz\"\n      ],\n      \"help\": \"Can be an assembled genome or transcriptome (DNA), or protein sequences from an annotated gene set.\",\n      \"help_format\": \"html\",\n      \"hidden\": false,\n      \"is_dynamic\": false,\n      \"label\": \"Sequences to analyse\",\n      \"model_class\": \"DataToolParameter\",\n      \"multiple\": false,\n      \"name\": \"input\",\n      \"optional\": false,\n      \"options\": {\n        \"dce\": [],\n        \"hda\": [\n          {\n            \"hid\": 4,\n            \"id\": \"f9cad7b01a4721353c9efc